  "body": "Phase 1I adds configuration-driven country profiles, scenario adjustments, capability availability and regulation applicability on the existing canonical context, knowledge, evidence, RuleHit and metadata contracts. Results retain stable status/reason codes, evidence and legal-basis references, immutable provenance and explicit snapshot/configuration pins. Capability availability does not decide legal obligations.\n\nMultilingual metadata supports zh-CN, zh-HK and en-US through one generic display contract stored in existing versioned metadata. Runtime metadata and applicability presenters resolve governed fallback without changing formal results, official sources or citations. Actor-scoped registry projection prevents restricted profiles or labels leaking across requests. No frontend language switcher, document translation, LLM gateway or Phase 1J implementation is included.\n\nMigration 0009_phase1i uses explicit DDL; frozen migrations 0001\u20130008 are byte-identical to the verified Phase 1H baseline 700951ebb9ebdf33e399158fd3fb53bb4a6c87e7. Shared persistence/admin/registry/gate extensions require integration review with parallel tracks; migration ownership must remain explicit.\n\nValidation:\n- Final implementation b2312e9ec48bd05e3398c23f79dcfcf1faf69b9f: full local PostgreSQL/runtime suite 356 passed, zero failures/errors/skips/deselections; 72 Phase 1I cases.\n- Fresh migration, exact baseline0008\u21920009 upgrade, schema equivalence, empty downgrade and retained-authority downgrade refusal PASS.\n- Phase 1B\u20131I schema regressions PASS; architecture135/135 and runtime25/25 PASS.\n- Exact final head 14cba25353d9ab7dda84e9620ff3197d9e2a3d1d: [remote CI37275070629](https://github.com/bensuen0831/crossborder-compliance-agent/actions/runs/37275070629) SUCCESS; contract-tests and mandatory-runtime-smoke SUCCESS.\n\nDelivery documents include integration_handoff.md (22 fields), i18n_metadata_backend_result.md, measured logs/manifests in evidence/phase1i, and Phase1J_entry_decision.md issued only after verified closure gates. Final remote job/artifact metadata is verified; signed artifact download was unavailable, so remote detailed test counts and complete-log hashes are not claimed. The cited 356 count is measured locally.\n\nKeep this PR DRAFT targeting main. No merge or post-merge baseline is claimed. Phase 1J requires a separately reviewed integration baseline and its own Start Gate.",
